    "body": "## Summary\n\nADR-038: **14 new pseudo-classes across three CSS categories**. Ships in one integrated commit (the ADR's 3-commit plan converged organically during implementation — the parser/matcher/specificity extensions were interleaved to keep tests green throughout; documented in commit message).\n\n## What ships\n\n### Structural (10 pseudos, ~38 rules)\n\n`:first-child`, `:last-child`, `:only-child`, `:empty`, `:first-of-type`, `:last-of-type`, `:only-of-type`, `:nth-child(An+B)`, `:nth-last-child(An+B)`, `:nth-of-type(An+B)`, `:nth-last-of-type(An+B)`\n\nAn+B grammar: `odd`, `even`, `N`, `An`, `An+B`, `-An+B` (whitespace variants accepted). Matcher uses element-only sibling index helpers per CSS spec.\n\n### Logical (3 pseudos, ~392 rules)\n\n`:not(compound-list)`, `:is(compound-list)`, `:where(compound-list)`\n\nCompound args supported (AND of simples). Combinator args dropped per CSS4 forgiving behavior. **`:where()` specificity is `0,0,0`** (whole point of `:where()` — reset-style rules that any class overrides); `:not()` / `:is()` take max of argument specificities.\n\n### Language (1 pseudo, ~410 rules)\n\n`:lang(tag)` — walks ancestor chain for first non-empty `lang` attribute. Case-insensitive BCP-47 prefix match: `:lang(en)` matches `lang=\"en\"` AND `lang=\"en-US\"`; `:lang(en-US)` does NOT match bare `lang=\"en\"`.\n\n## The measurement that justified the scope\n\n| Category | Rules on Wikipedia |\n|---|---|\n| `:lang()` | **410** |\n| `:not()` | **374** |\n| `:where()` | 16 |\n| `:is()` | 2 |\n| Structural (all) | 38 |\n| **Total** | **~840** |\n\n**`:nth-child()` — the headline of the original structural-only scope — has ZERO uses in Wikipedia's CSS.** The ADR title changed from \"Structural pseudo-classes\" to \"Pseudo-Class Expansion\" mid-cycle to match what measurement showed. Scope amendment documented in ADR's Context section.\n\n## Honest caveats\n\n1. **`:nth-child()` has zero uses in Wikipedia CSS** — ships for spec completeness, tested synthetically\n2. **`:lang()` visible delta on English Wikipedia is zero** — the test article is `lang=\"en\"`; language-specific rules don't match. Infrastructure for non-English pages\n3. **`:has()` still dropped** (8 rules stay not-matching) — ADR-039 (descendant traversal, different complexity)\n4. **`:dir()` still dropped** — 1 use, inside `:has()`, same deferral\n5. **Form-state pseudos** (`:focus`, `:active`, `:checked`, `:enabled`, etc.) still dropped — separate category, own ADR\n6. **One selector-parser test transitioned** — `:first-child` and `:not(.x)` now parse; test renamed, input changed to `:checked` (still-unsupported form-state pseudo). Same pattern as ADR-029's \"display_of unknown value\" test\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before: 456 cases / 1792 assertions\n- After: **480 cases / 1851 assertions** (+24 / +59)\n- Full suite all pass, zero warnings\n\nNew `tests/test_pseudos.cpp` (23 tests):\n- 13 structural: all 10 forms + An+B grammar + `:empty` whitespace\n- 6 logical: `:not` inversion, compound args, `:is` either, `:where` zero-specificity, `:not` specificity\n- 4 `:lang`: exact match, prefix match, no-overreach, no-lang-anywhere\n\nUpdated `tests/test_selectors.cpp`:\n- `:first-child` moved from \"unknown\" to supported test\n- `:not(.x)` moved from \"unknown\" to supported\n- `:checked` replaces them in the \"unknown pseudo\" test (form-state, still genuinely unknown)\n\n## What this unblocks (cascade-level)\n\n| | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Pseudo-classes supported | 4 (`:link`/`:visited`/`:hover`/`:root`) | **18** |\n| Wikipedia CSS rules participating in cascade | ~450 (dropped ~840) | **~1290** |\n| `:not()` theme/state rules | dropped | apply |\n| `:first-child`/`:last-child` spacing | dropped | apply |\n| `:lang()` language-specific rules | dropped | apply (zero delta on en, ready for other locales) |\n\n## What's next\n\n- **ADR-039**: `:has()` + `:dir()` (descendant traversal, next complexity class)\n- **ADR-040**: form-state pseudos (`:focus`, `:active`, `:checked`, `:enabled`, `:disabled`, `:read-only`) — own category\n- **Pseudo-elements** (`:before` / `:after` + `content`) — ADR candidate, high visible potential (60-69 uses)\n\nRefs #194\n",
